dialog: Give each dialog an identity and own its focus restore

- Window::active_dialog_handle returns a DialogHandle (focus handle plus
  liveness), and Window::close_dialog_if closes exactly that dialog, even
  when another dialog covers it. Code that opened a dialog can close its
  own one without closing whatever is on top.
- Each delayed focus restoration has its own identity. Before, a timer that
  compared dialog counts could focus a dialog that replaced the old one at
  the same depth, or clear a newer pending restoration.

Remove when upstream offers owner-scoped closing and restoration ownership.

